{
 "about": "Door gauges for the four-view building art (scripts/assets/prep-views.mjs). door = the height in native pixels of a plain single-leaf door (a house front door, a shop back or side door; glazed shopfront doors are left out, they are drawn taller), read on the leaf edge from under the head casing to the threshold. A view is scaled so its door stands standardDoor game px tall at the building owner scale; a view with no clear plain door takes the mean scale of its measured views; a version with no measured view keeps the original sprite width (noGauge marks a subject with nothing to measure). Business artwork is drawn at a share of its parcel, so it keeps its original width and takes no gauge. The sha256 ties each reading to the exact picture: a regenerated picture is unmeasured until re-read.",
